The hotel is located directly on Riverwalk on Market Street. The interior is beautiful; check-in was efficient and friendly. Rooms are well appointed and I absolutely love the bed and pillow at this Westin, I had two an incredible nights’ sleep. The bathroom was absolutely spotless, which is a huge bonus for any location. The HDTV was better than most and did not pixelate at all. The fitness center was excellent; 4 ellipticals, 4 cycles, and 8 treadmills, all first rate and in excellent condition. There are two benches for the free weights and one weight machine that allows for 20+ different exercises. The phical plant of this location is one of the nicest of the brand.
There are some process improvements that I would recommend to create even a better experience. 
• As a Platinum member I asked for an upgrade as part of my earned benefits. The front desk felt that a view of the river was a better option than a suite with a city view. I recommend that they ask the guest which they prefer since I would and did opt for the latter;
• The internet wireless service has three levels of speed that you choose when you first log in. Even with the highest speed I was required to re-start several times as pages would not load. Just be aware that the “handshake” can be lost often while on the wireless in the room. Waiting for someone from technical support to answer the phone was a long process and you need to be patient until someone picks up; 
• Coffee is available in the room via the mini machines but not in the lobby and the hotel does not have a lounge area. There is a Starbucks that opens at 6:30;
• The valet parking ($30 per night) is a broken process. It is the only location I know that takes your ticket every time you leave (strange that they focus on “green” yet the exchange is a waste of paper). Then when you return you have to sit and wait, then give your name and room number for a different ticket. I recommend that they do as the other 99.9% of the hotels do, just leave the same ticket for the entire stay. 
• The keys are electronic and during my stay two keys failed. The first occurred after I was rushed into the hotel during some police activity outside and I just wanted the safety of my room; the second occurred after exercising at 630 am, and I was glad the front desk clerk did not ask me for ID. 
• Zocca – Breakfast includes both a Continental and a Full Buffet plus a la carte from the menu. The Continental (only cold) buffet included boxed cereal (thankfully it included my favorite low-fat Granola) fruits, and breads. My only comment, which I conveyed to the MOD was that guests should be asked if they wanted to be seated inside or on the Riverwalk, outside. I was immediately shuffled to an interior table and likewise a party of 2 was initially shown a table inside and had to ask to be seated at one of the vacant tables overlooking the river.
Overall, this is a fantastic location and the physical property is gorgeous and well maintained, housekeeping was outstanding and the fitness center was top notch. There are a few processes that should be addressed. The General Manager did reach out to me and we had a productive conversation about the POV from a customer and how to make this hotel even better. On my next trip to San Antonio, this is definitely the place to stay.

After spending three nights at the Hotel del Coronado, I moved to the Marriott Liberty Station the night before an early morning flight. Frankly, my stay here was better than the Hotel del:
- the rooms were well appointed, spacious, new and clean;
- there was no charge for parking, nor was there a resort fee;
- the Internet access was speedy;
- I was easily able to print off my boarding pass for free;
- the pool area was clean;
- the staff was friendly; and
- it was great value for the cost.
The only negative: I did hear jet noise from planes landing, but it wasn't too bad. I would recommend this hotel to others staying in the area.
